DIAGNOSTIC: make a rejected command stream say where it was rejected.

The generated protocol decoders call vn_cs_decoder_set_fatal() from 1358
places and none of them log anything.  Most are a switch default over a
pNext chain -- "unexpected struct" -- so a guest sending an extension the
host's generated decoder predates fails with no explanation: the only
output is the dispatcher's "<command> resulted in CS error", which names
the command but not the reason.  That is what CK3 produces here on
vkCreateGraphicsPipelines.

Route every call through a wrapper that reports __func__ first.  Decoder
names are generated from the structure being decoded, so "CS decode
rejected in vn_decode_VkGraphicsPipelineCreateInfo_pnext_temp" identifies
the exact chain that was refused.

fprintf is used rather than vkr_log because this header only pulls in
vkr_cs.h; the render server's stderr already reaches the VMM log.

--- src/venus/venus-protocol/vn_protocol_renderer_cs.h.orig
+++ src/venus/venus-protocol/vn_protocol_renderer_cs.h
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #define VN_PROTOCOL_RENDERER_CS_H
 
 #include <assert.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
 
 /*
  * These types/functions are expected
@@ -63,11 +64,15 @@
 }
 
 static inline void
-vn_cs_decoder_set_fatal(const struct vn_cs_decoder *dec)
+vn_cs_decoder_set_fatal_at(const struct vn_cs_decoder *dec, const char *fn)
 {
    const struct vkr_cs_decoder *d = (struct vkr_cs_decoder *)dec;
+   fprintf(stderr, "vkr: CS decode rejected in %s\n", fn);
    vkr_cs_decoder_set_fatal(d);
 }
+
+/* Every generated call site becomes self-identifying. */
+#define vn_cs_decoder_set_fatal(dec) vn_cs_decoder_set_fatal_at((dec), __func__)
 
 static inline bool
 vn_cs_decoder_get_fatal(const struct vn_cs_decoder *dec)
